# Travis Picking (repertoire plan: st-travis-picking). An original 16-bar study: C, C, Am, Am,
# G7, G7, C, C, played twice. The thumb (P) plays every beat and alternates two bass strings,
# lightly palm muted:
#   C (x32010): string 5 fret 3 (C), string 4 fret 2 (E), string 6 fret 3 (G), string 4 fret 2
#               (finger 3 hops between strings 5 and 6);
#   Am (x02210): the open string 5 (A) and string 4 fret 2 (E);
#   G7 (320001): string 6 fret 3 (G) and the open string 4 (D).
# Between the thumb notes, i plucks string 2 on the "and" of 1 and 3, and m plucks string 1 on
# the "and" of 2 and 4. Bars 9-16 are the same with a pinch on beat 1: thumb and m together.
title: Travis Picking
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original fingerstyle study
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 4
tags: travis picking, alternating bass, fingerstyle, thumb
tempo: 80
time: 4/4
key: C

track: Your part
role: lead
[Thumb and fingers]
| "C=x32010" e 5:3{P 3 pm} 2:1{I 1} 4:2{P 2 pm} 1:0{M} 6:3{P 3 pm} 2:1{I} 4:2{P pm} 1:0{M} | 5:3{pm} 2:1 4:2{pm} 1:0 6:3{pm} 2:1 4:2{pm} 1:0 |
